{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-56-1","title":"Isaiah 56:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The prophet exhorts to sanctification. 3 He promises it shall be general, without respect of persons. 9 He inveighs against blind watchmen.</p>\n<p>Keep. 1:16-19; 26:7,8; 55:7; Ps 24:4-6; 50:23; Jer 7:3-11; Mal 4:4 Mt 3:2; Joh 7:17 judgment. or, equity. for. 46:13; 51:5; Ps 85:9; Mt 3:2; 4:17; Mr 1:15; Lu 3:3-9; Ro 1:17 Ro 10:6-10; 13:11-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-2","title":"Isaiah 56:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Blessed. Ps 1:1-3; 15:1-5; 106:3; 112:1; 119:1-5; 128:1; Lu 11:28; 12:43 Joh 13:17; Re 22:14 layeth. 4; Pr 4:13; Ec 7:18 keepeth the. 58:13; Ex 31:13-16; Le 19:30; Ne 13:17; Jer 17:21,22; Eze 20:12,20 keepeth his. Ps 34:14; 37:27; 119:101; Pr 4:27; 14:16; 16:6,17; Ro 12:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-3","title":"Isaiah 56:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the son. Nu 18:4,7; De 23:1-3; Zec 8:20-23; Mt 8:10,11; Ac 8:27; 10:1,2,34 Ac 13:47,48; 17:4; 18:7; Ro 2:10,11; 15:9-12,16; Eph 2:12,22 1Pe 1:1 joined. Jer 50:5; Zep 2:11; 1Co 6:17 The Lord hath. Mt 15:26,27; Lu 7:6-8 neither. 5; 39:7; Jer 38:7-13; 39:16,17; Da 1:3-21; Mt 19:12-30; Ac 8:26-40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-4","title":"Isaiah 56:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>choose. Jos 24:15; Ps 119:111; Lu 10:42 take hold. 27:5; 55:3; 2Sa 23:5; Jer 50:5; Heb 6:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-5","title":"Isaiah 56:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>will I. Mt 16:18; Eph 2:22; 1Ti 3:15; Heb 3:6 and a. 62:12; Joh 1:12; 1Jo 3:1; Re 3:12 better. 1Sa 1:8 that shall. 55:13; Re 3:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-6","title":"Isaiah 56:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>join. 3; 44:5; Jer 50:5; Ac 2:41; 11:23; 2Co 8:5; 1Th 1:9,10 to love. Mr 12:30-34; Ro 8:28; 1Co 16:22; Ga 5:6; Eph 6:24; Jas 1:12; 2:5 every. 2; 58:13; Re 1:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-7","title":"Isaiah 56:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>them will. 2:2,3; 66:19,20; Ps 2:6; Mic 4:1,2; Zec 8:3; Mal 1:11; Joh 12:20-26 Eph 2:11-13; Heb 12:22; 1Pe 1:1,2 their burnt. Ro 12:1; Heb 13:15; 1Pe 2:5 for mine. Mal 1:11; Mt 21:13; Mr 11:17; Lu 19:46; Joh 4:21-23; 1Ti 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-8","title":"Isaiah 56:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>which. 11:11,12; 27:12,13; 54:7; Ps 106:47; 107:2,3; 147:2; Jer 30:17 Jer 31:10; Ho 1:11; Mic 4:6; Zep 3:18-20; Zec 10:8-10 Yet. 43:6; 49:12,22; 60:3-11; 66:18-21; Ge 49:10; Joh 10:16; 11:52 Eph 1:10; 2:14-16 beside those that are gathered. Heb. to his gathered.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-9","title":"Isaiah 56:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>De 28:26; Jer 12:9; Eze 29:5; 39:17; Re 19:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-10","title":"Isaiah 56:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>watchmen. 52:8; Eze 3:17 are blind. 29:10; Jer 14:13,14; Ho 4:6; 9:7,8; Mt 15:14; 23:16-26; Lu 6:39,40 they are all dumb. 58:1; Jer 6:13,14; 23:13,14; Eze 3:15-18,26,27; 13:16; 33:6 Php 3:2 sleeping. or, dreaming, or talking in their sleep. loving. Pr 6:4-10; 24:30-34; Jon 1:2-6; Na 3:18; Mr 13:34-37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-11","title":"Isaiah 56:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Yea, they are. 1Sa 2:12-17,29; Eze 13:19; 34:2,3; Mic 3:5,11; Mal 1:10 Ac 20:29,33; Php 3:2,19; 1Ti 3:3,8; Tit 1:7,11; 1Pe 5:2 2Pe 2:3,14,15; Jude 1:11,16; Re 22:15 greedy. Heb. strong of appetite. can never have enough.Heb. know not to be satisfied. Ec 5:10 are shepherds. Mic 3:6; Zec 11:15-17; Mt 13:14,15; Joh 8:43; 2Co 4:4 all look. Ex 23:3; Jer 22:17; 2Pe 2:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-56-12","title":"Isaiah 56:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":56,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":56,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>I will. 5:22; 28:7,8; Pr 31:4,5; Ho 4:11; Am 6:3-6; Mt 24:49-51 Lu 12:45,46; 21:34; Tit 1:7 to morrow. 22:13,14; Ps 10:6; Pr 23:35; 27:1; Jer 18:18; Lu 12:19,20 1Co 15:32</p>"}]}